; Rushing Beat Shura — BRAZILIAN-PORTUGUESE (pt-BR) encoding table.
; PK font 8x16 with the tight-8 renderer patch at $05839F (chars occupy a
; single tile column). Latin set as tables/rbshura_en.tbl, with two pt-BR
; differences: the Portuguese accents at slots 0x4C..0x58, and the COLON moved
; off slot 0x20 — 0x20 is now a SPACE (the PK font shipped a colon glyph there,
; which made spaces render as colons), and ':' lives at slot 0x59.
;
; STATUS: the accents (0x4C..0x58), the blanked 0x20 (space), and the relocated
; ':' (0x59) all live in the relocated/extended font at $E2:0000
; (fonts/rbshura_font_ext.bin, 90 slots), because the original 80-slot region at
; $100000 is full. The dialogue + intro + narration renderers have their font
; base repointed $D0->$E2 (patches/font_reloc.asm + narration_render.asm). Built
; and audit-clean; pending in-emulator verification. Regenerate the glyphs with
; tools/make_pt_accents.py; edit them visually with tools/font_png.py.

@ctrl_prefix F7 F8 F9 FB FC FD FE FF
@ctrl F7=2
@ctrl F8=2
@ctrl F9=2
@ctrl FB=2
@ctrl FC=3
@ctrl FC.02=4
@ctrl FD=1
@ctrl FE=1
@ctrl FF=1

